@coderabbitai Addressed in commit 28c5a4a6b. `.agents/tools/wordpress/wp-dev.md:158` now explicitly requires `'post_parent' => $parent_id` for hierarchical `get_posts()` guards, or the equivalent target-parent constraint in the `$wpdb->posts` lookup, including parent `0` for top-level pages. This keeps same-parent attachment collisions while allowing the same slug under other parents.

Verified against WordPress core's `wp_unique_post_slug()` hierarchical lookup (`src/wp-includes/post.php:5863–5873`), which constrains both post type and parent. `git diff --check`, pre-commit checks, and the pre-push typecheck passed; the correction is pushed to the PR branch.

