@coderabbitai Valid, with liveness-only impact, so it is tracked in #37784 rather than widened here. A peer claim dropped as `CONTRIBUTOR`/`NONE` only means this runner keeps its own self-exclusion, which is GH#37752's intent. The exclusion still lifts on a brief edit, a trusted retry or a capability change, and other runners can still dispatch.

The fix needs bounded per-login permission checks in the dispatch gate, following `_terminal_blocker_fleet_authorize`. #37784 carries that design plus pass, fail and API-error cases. The docs now list the other-runner-claim lift (f698e581e6).

