@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM62USGc -->
Addressed: `.agents/scripts/pulse-merge.sh:1423` now classifies a fresh exact-head snapshot before deferring active CI, and `:1515` does the same before the native-auto path can return. Terminal failures use the existing CI repair route with the snapshot's explicit failure JSON; pending-only CI retains native deferral, while a changed head stays blocked without repair against stale evidence. This does not restore the full authority/review gate in pre-merge.

Verified with `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-pulse-merge-ci-repair-routing.sh` (including newly failed, mixed active/failing, pending-only, and head-race cases), the snapshot/native-auto/ruleset suites, and ShellCheck.

@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM62USGi -->
Addressed: timing now lives inside `_pulse_merge_final_trust_gate` (`.agents/scripts/pulse-merge.sh:778`), so every native/admin/direct invocation, blocked gate, fallback, and stale-auth retry contributes to the same `trust_gate_s` accumulator. Removed the caller-specific admin timer to avoid double-counting.

Verified with `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-pulse-merge-timing-summary.sh`: deterministic cumulative durations cover every blocking stage, successful gates, a real native-auto enable, and telemetry-disabled behavior. Native-auto and ruleset fallback suites plus ShellCheck also pass.

@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM62XUlt -->
Addressed in `.agents/scripts/pulse-merge.sh:785`: the final gate now clears blocking-check JSON before authority, review, and worker-briefed checks. An early failure cannot route evidence retained from another PR; the current snapshot can still populate and route fresh evidence.

Extended `test-pulse-merge-timing-summary.sh:183` to seed stale evidence before each failure and exercise the actual admin gate/routing helpers. Authority, review, and worker-briefed failures clear it without dispatch; a snapshot failure routes only its fresh evidence. Verified the timing/isolation, CI repair routing, and ruleset fallback suites, ShellCheck, and `git diff --check`.

@coderabbitai Addressed in commit 2911a0b1d. `.agents/services/hosting/cloudron.md:162` now makes both default-certificate selection and a TLS name mismatch conditional; the installed-app check guidance is unchanged.

